num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**The creation/redemption arbitrage mechanism** keeps ETF prices aligned with NAV.\n\n**How it works:**\n- **Authorized Participants (APs)**, usually large broker-dealers, create or redeem ETF shares directly with the issuer in large blocks (\"creation units,\" often 10,000–50,000 shares).\n- **Premium (price > NAV):** APs buy the underlying securities, exchange them for new ETF shares, and sell those on the exchange. Added supply pushes the price down.\n- **Discount (price < NAV):** APs buy cheap ETF shares, redeem them for the underlying basket, and sell the basket. Reduced supply lifts the price.\n\n**Supporting factors:**\n- **Transparency:** Daily holdings disclosure and real-time iNAV help market makers price fair value.\n- **Competitive market makers** narrow spreads.\n- **Liquid underlying assets** make arbitrage cheap and fast.\n\n**When it weakens:** Premiums and discounts can widen with illiquid holdings (high-yield bonds, frontier markets), during market stress, or when underlying markets are closed.","ttft_ms":1579,"type":"result","duration_ms":4248,"uuid":"6f0ae9a6-5130-4eeb-9d83-2c4fbef293ef","ttft_stream_ms":1074,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1074,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
